Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the use of guest physical addresses that overlapped with a reserved address range defined by HyperTransport on AMD processors. This overlap could lead to failures during self-tests, particularly when the maximum guest frame number (gfn) was calculated without accounting for these reserved addresses, especially on processors with different physical address bit configurations and Secure Memory Encryption (SME) settings.

